<title>USA: Santer says no reason to worry about French on EMU.</title>
<headline>Santer says no reason to worry about French on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer said on Friday he saw no reason to worry about the approach of France's new Socialist-led government to European economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;I understand from the French side, and Prime Minister Lionel Jospin said this in Amsterdam, that he is sticking to the single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;They do their utmost to enter monetary union, there is no reason for nervousness at this moment.&quot;</p>
<p>He also said the euro would be a strong currency, otherwise member states would oppose it.</p>
<p>&quot;The euro will be a strong currency,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
